.TH PANORA-GUI 1 "2026-09-19" "panora" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
panora-gui, panora \- Panora clipboard history popup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B panora
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.br
.B panora-gui
.RB [ \-\-gapplication\-service ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B panora-gui
is the GTK4/libadwaita panel that shows the clipboard history recorded by
.BR panod (1):
search as you type, filter by type (text, link, image, file, rich text,
colour, pinned), pin, delete, inspect an entry and put it back on the
clipboard. It is a single-instance application: launching it while the panel
is open closes the panel, which is what Super+V, the launcher entry and
.B panora-cli toggle
rely on.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Focus the search box.
.TP
.B Up, Down, Left, Right
Move between entries.
.TP
.B Enter
Put the selected entry on the clipboard (and paste it when instant paste is
enabled), then close.
.TP
.B Space
Open the details view (full text, full-size image, formats).
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
Pin or unpin the selected entry.
.TP
.B Delete
Delete the selected entry.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+P
Toggle private mode.
.TP
.B Ctrl+,
Open settings.
.TP
.B Esc
Clear the search; close when the search is empty.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-gapplication\-service
Start as a D-Bus service without showing a window (used by D-Bus activation).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/panora/config.toml
Settings written by the preferences dialog.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR panod (1),
.BR panora-cli (1)
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/ygkali/panora/issues
